	(text "REGEN SHUNT (record section 5). Self-acting clamp: comparator + reference + FET, no firmware in the loop. Threshold ~45 V ON, a few volts hysteresis.\nThat is above the GST360A36 worst-case 37.8 V OVP trip, legal ONLY because the input section blocks reverse current: the supply never sees the bus rise. Sizing ~7 W continuous / ~150 W peak (motor switch removes the unpowered case).\nR11 || R12: two TO-263 on top over 0.8 mm via fields into the back sink (stackup.md). 16R each = 8R total, the value that holds the bus (section 5).\nJ3 + JP1: external resistor. JP1 bridged = parallel with the on-board pair; cut JP1 = external replaces it. Size Q6 for the lowest combined R.\nD1 across the switch node: external flying leads add inductance whose energy lands on Q6's drain at turn-off.\nCLAMP_MON: gate divided to 3.3 V for a GPIO; duty x V^2 / R = shunt dissipation, no second INA (section 12).\nSupplied from +12V: the 12 V buck starts from the bus by itself, so the clamp stays firmware-free. TODO(detailing): divider values, hysteresis, SHDN pin, pulse energy vs PWR263S curve (SPEC open item)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
